  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Peel the cucumber into ribbons with a vegetable peeler. Thinly slice the radish with a sharp knife or mandoline. Thinly slice the spring onion. Cut the tofu into 2cm-thick slices.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1566568/photos/large/prep_ingredients-f9da0f671cbcd7be984933e790c33383.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pickle veggies: Put the cucumber, radish and 2 tsp white vinegar in a large bowl, season with salt and pepper and toss to combine. Set aside to pickle, tossing occasionally, until needed.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1566569/photos/large/pickle_veggies-cdc77bda3e117bcd406fd144b9d85b1d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tofu: Put the sunflower seeds in a cold medium frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 2-3 mins until evenly golden. Remove from the pan. Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in the same pan over medium heat. Cook the tofu for 2 mins each side or until golden and warmed through. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1566570/photos/large/prepare_tofu-f54f362780a7c8389554bfef43147c1d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make salad: Drain the pickled veggies, discarding the pickling liquid, then return to the bowl. Add the salad leaves and Japanese dressing and toss to combine. Put 2 tbs mayonnaise (see Make it yours) and 2 tsp water in a separate bowl, season with salt and pepper and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1566571/photos/large/warm_tofu-8d98da80618eebe911cb4e31a041409d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the salad among bowls and top with the tofu. Drizzle with the mayonnaise mixture, scatter over the spring onion and sunflower seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1566572/photos/large/serve_up-d04a083041ed62a8871e6f7fb20cf23e.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: The mayonnaise drizzle adds a creamy element to the tofu salad, but if you prefer to leave it out the dish will still be delicious!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/1566573/photos/large/make_it_yours-6157e5ca7b66b61c43ff509e1005a6f0.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
